# Simultaneous Frobenius class from faithful Galois characters

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.disjointRamification_seededFrobeniusClass_exists_v4`
(`6eddaf9a-6e8c-497f-b780-ea0879245886`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25.

Proof: submission `c1b35dba-8456-4200-8608-1bf75bda9c3c`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25
(SKETCH_ACCEPTED); locally adapted.

Combine the residual representation with faithful cyclotomic and seed Galois-character data.
Disjoint ramification supplies a Chebotarev class with trivial residual and cyclotomic components
and a full-order seed component.

## Explanation of the source proof

Construct the residual Galois representation attached to the eigenform and use its ramification
theorem to see that every prime dividing the kernel-field discriminant divides $Np$. The faithful
seed/cyclotomic realization supplies a residue class on which the seed character has full order.

The already proved coprime-discriminant theorem applies because the seed conductor is coprime to
$Np$. It produces the required Chebotarev conjugacy class, hence the bundled
`SeededOrderlyFrobeniusClassData`. The remaining open child is the standard textbook existence
theorem for the residual eigenform representation; all ramification, cyclotomic, and assembly steps
are proved nodes on the clean spine.

